    <node id="吴国">
      <data key="d0">吴国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">The State of Wu (吴国) was a historical entity known for its rivalry with the State of Yue (越国). It was ruled by King Fu Chai (吴王夫差) and is notable for its strategic military engagements against Yue. The State of Wu was also recognized for its expertise in sword-making, boasting skilled craftsmen in this area, which played a significant role in its military capabilities.

Wu was the destination for prominent figures such as Fan Li (范蠡) and Wen Zhong (文种), who were associated with the state's governance and military strategies. The state heavily relied on the talents of military strategist Wu Zixu (伍子胥), who was instrumental in its military campaigns and political maneuvers.

In addition to its military endeavors, Wu engaged in diplomatic relations, sending envoys to negotiate with Yue. The interactions between Wu and Yue included notable conflicts, such as those involving a character named A Qing (阿青), who had confrontations with Wu's swordsmen. These encounters highlight the tensions and hostilities that characterized the relationship between the two states.

Overall, the State of Wu is remembered for its military prowess, strategic leadership, and its ongoing conflict with the State of Yue, which shaped its historical narrative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66</data>
