    <node id="越国">
      <data key="d0">越国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity 越国, known as the State of Yue, was historically significant as the kingdom ruled by the legendary figure 勾践 (Gou Jian). This state is particularly noted for its rivalry with the neighboring State of Wu, with which it had a deeply entrenched enmity. The conflicts between 越国 and 吴国 (Wu) are well-documented, highlighting a long-standing adversarial relationship.

In addition to its military and political significance, 越国 is also associated with notable historical figures such as 范蠡 (Fan Li) and 文种 (Wen Zhong), who were prominent advisors and strategists in the court of 勾践. They are known to have traveled to 越国, where 勾践 received them, indicating the state's importance as a center of political activity and strategy during its time.

Furthermore, 越国 is recognized for its cultural contributions, including the martial arts of 阿青 (A Qing), whose swordsmanship gained attention within the kingdom. This aspect underscores the state's role not only in military affairs but also in the cultural development of the region.

Overall, 越国 is characterized by its historical significance as a rival to 吴国, its association with key historical figures, and its contributions to martial arts and culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66</data>
